### All events
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events

### One event
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/1

### Missing event -> 404
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/999

### Search by title (ignoring case)
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events?title=quiz

### Search with no matches -> []
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events?title=football

### Optional: title + location filters
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events?title=workshop&location=room

### Create -> 201, note the returned id (here assumed 4)
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Spring Data Workshop",
  "location": "IITU, Room 101"
}

### Update id 4 -> 200, id stays the same
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/events/4
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Spring Data JPA Workshop",
  "location": "IITU, Main Hall"
}

### Check the update
GET http://localhost:8080/api/events/4

### Delete id 4 -> 204 (repeat -> 404)
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/events/4

### Update a missing id -> 404
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/events/999
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Any",
  "location": "Any"
}

### Delete a missing id -> 404
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/events/999

### Empty title -> 400, no row is created
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "location": "Room 101"
}

### Client-provided id is ignored -> 201 with a database-generated id
POST http://localhost:8080/api/events
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "id": 777,
  "title": "Id Test",
  "location": "Room 1"
}
